A turn on lent time whose thread's place there goes is not charged first,
so the lender pays nothing for what the borrower ran before, and runs it free;
a turn is charged as the units it runs on change, its own place's too.

Caught-by: fuzz-smp2
Report: a place counted overruns otherwise than as a charge reached a request's end
Witness: fuzz-smp2 cores-lend-borrower-unbound

diff --git a/kernel/sched.c b/kernel/sched.c
--- a/kernel/sched.c
+++ b/kernel/sched.c
@@ -643,7 +643,7 @@ static void place_charge(struct place *p)
 {
     const struct thread *t = place_thread(p);
     struct core *core = &cores[t->core];
-    if (is_turn(t) && (turn_place(core) == p || turn_own(core) == p)) {
+    if (is_turn(t) && turn_place(core) == p) {
         turn_charge(core);
     }
 }
